nt.mp3","establish":"audio/w/establish.mp3","The university was established in the nineteenth century.":"audio/e/establish.mp3","estimate":"audio/w/estimate.mp3","Scientists estimate that the universe is fourteen billion years old.":"audio/e/estimate.mp3","evident":"audio/w/evident.mp3","It is evident that the policy has failed.":"audio/e/evident.mp3","export":"audio/w/export.mp3","Coal remains one of Australia's major exports.":"audio/e/export.mp3","factor":"audio/w/factor.mp3","Diet is an important factor in overall health.":"audio/e/factor.mp3","finance":"audio/w/finance.mp3","The project was financed by the government.":"audio/e/finance.mp3","formula":"audio/w/formula.mp3","There is no simple formula for success.":"audio/e/formula.mp3","For most of the twentieth century, city planners assumed that fresh water would always be available when people turned on the tap.":"audio/a/d01a-1.mp3","That assumption is now being questioned.":"audio/a/d01a-2.mp3","When researchers analysed data from more than two hundred large cities, they estimated that one in four already faces regular water shortages.":"audio/a/d01a-3.mp3","It is evident that climate is only one factor.":"audio/a/d01a-4.mp3","Population growth, ageing pipes and poor planning also play a part.":"audio/a/d01a-5.mp3","In many places, water is not distributed fairly: wealthy suburbs receive a steady supply, while poorer districts depend on trucks and wells.":"audio/a/d01a-6.mp3","Local authorities have tried several approaches.":"audio/a/d01a-7.mp3","Some have built desalination plants, which turn sea water into drinking water but use large amounts of energy.":"audio/a/d01a-8.mp3","Others have invested in recycling waste water for farms and factories.":"audio/a/d01a-9.mp3","Cape Town, for example, cut its consumption by almost half during a severe drought by limiting each household to fifty litres a day.":"audio/a/d01a-10.mp3","Experts argue that cities must assess the true cost of each option, including its impact on the environment.":"audio/a/d01a-11.mp3","A plant that supplies water cheaply today may damage marine life for decades.":"audio/a/d01a-12.mp3","The greatest benefit, many suggest, comes from simple measures: fixing leaks, charging fair prices and teaching people to value every drop.":"audio/a/d01a-13.mp3","A cup of coffee may seem simple, but the concept of its price is surprisingly complex.":"audio/a/d01b-1.mp3","The final cost consists of many parts: the beans, transport, roasting, rent, wages and tax.":"audio/a/d01b-2.mp3","Growers, who do most of the hard work, often receive less than ten percent of what the customer pays.":"audio/a/d01b-3.mp3","To understand why, we need some historical context.":"audio/a/d01b-4.mp3","Coffee was first grown as an export crop in colonies, where the economy was designed to send raw materials to Europe.":"audio/a/d01b-5.mp3","Many producing countries still derive a large share of their national income from coffee, yet they have little control over its price, which is set on international markets.":"audio/a/d01b-6.mp3","Because prices change so much, farmers struggle to plan ahead or obtain finance.":"audio/a/d01b-7.mp3","Some have formed cooperatives and signed long-term contracts with buyers.":"audio/a/d01b-8.mp3","Fair trade organisations have established a minimum price that protects growers when the market falls.":"audio/a/d01b-9.mp3","However, there is no simple formula for fairness.":"audio/a/d01b-10.mp3","Critics point out that it is hard to define a fair price, and that certification fees can be expensive for small farms.":"audio/a/d01b-11.mp3","Still, these schemes constitute an important step.":"audio/a/d01b-12.mp3","They remind consumers that every cup connects them to a long chain of people, and that the choices they make at the counter can shape lives on the other side of the world.":"audio/a/d01b-13.mp3","function":"audio/w/function.mp3","The main function of the heart is to pump blood.":"audio/e/function.mp3